From: Arctic
Subject: [PATCH] ntos: the services of NT's executive and its thread callout

The executive of NT is in the kernel (drivers/ntos, docs/ntos.md): its system
services before win32k's (0xf00), its callout in do_exit next to win32k's,
and what it needs of the kernel's own: an inotify instance in no process's
table (its events read into a kernel buffer), a thread's debug registers as
ptrace has them, ntsync objects made and changed by a caller that keeps their
files itself, a terminal's tty.

diff -ruN a/arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl b/arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl
--- a/arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl	2026-11-22 16:35:40.926327400 +0100
+++ b/arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscall_64.tbl	2026-11-22 16:36:42.183323500 +0100
@@ -443,8 +443,18 @@
 # not special and are not to be used for x32-specific syscalls.
 
 #
-# Arctic: win32k's services, from 0x1000 as the service table of win32k.sys
-# in Windows (drivers/win32k, docs/win32k.md)
+# Arctic: the services of NT's executive from 0xf00 (drivers/ntos, docs/ntos.md)
+# and win32k's from 0x1000, as the service tables of win32k.sys in Windows
+# (drivers/win32k, docs/win32k.md)
+#
+3840	64	nt_hello		sys_nt_hello
+3841	64	nt_call			sys_nt_call
+3842	64	nt_send_fd		sys_nt_send_fd
+3843	64	nt_receive_fd		sys_nt_receive_fd
+3844	64	nt_boot			sys_nt_boot
+3845	64	nt_admin		sys_nt_admin
+#
+# Arctic: win32k's services, as above
 #
 4096	64	win32k_hello		sys_win32k_hello
 4097	64	win32k_call		sys_win32k_call
